
All relevant documentation on compiling and running DEGAS 2 is now
contained in the manual. See the section there entitled "Compiling DEGAS 2".
The manual can be found at:

1. In text form as a TeX file in Doc/degas2_all.tex,
2. This directory also contains HTML, PostScript, and PDF versions
   of this same file.
3. These are all accessible via the Web from the URL:

   http://w3.pppl.gov/degas2

DEGAS 2  usage is now governed by a licensing procedure.  Interested
users should go to: 

http://theorycodes.pppl.wikispaces.net/Theory+Department+Codes

and fill out the form linked there.

DEGAS 2 is maintained with the Git version control system 
(http://git-scm.com/).   The version of this distribution
can be uniquely identified by a 40 character hexadecimal
"hash":  $Format:%H$.
One or more human readable references or tags may also
be used to label this version:  $Format:%d$.


